## Checks the applier must leave true
- `template` is single-quoted exactly as given, so the `{limit:number}`
  braces are literal YAML text and not a flow mapping.
- `block: then` — the step sits in the Then block of E2E-001 (the
  leading `and ` of `and the service answers within 200 milliseconds`
  is the block's continuation marker, not part of the step text, which
  is why the finding quotes the step without it). The template must not
  include `and `.
- No collision: the new template requires the literal words `within`
  and `milliseconds` and a `{limit:number}` slot (digits, or the word
  `no`), whereas `the service answers "{reply}"` requires a
  double-quoted run immediately after `answers`. No step can match
  both, and no other existing entry starts with `the service answers
  within`. Every step of E2E-001 still matches exactly one template:
  - `the mcp service is running` → `'the mcp service is running'` (given)
  - `the Operator sends "ping"` → `'the {actor:role} sends "{message}"'` (when; `Operator` is a `roles[].name`)
  - `the service answers "pong"` → `'the service answers "{reply}"'` (then)
  - `the service answers within 200 milliseconds` → the new entry (then)
- Both `terms` entries are spelled exactly as the glossary spells them:
  `mcp service` and `reply`. Do not add, rename or re-word any glossary
  term — both already exist.
- Nothing else in `docs/product/product.yaml` changes: same `title`,
  `description`, `roles`, `glossary`, and the first three catalogue
